# Cloudflare Pages custom headers — tsigalogo.gr
#
# WHY: Pages' default asset TTL is only 4h (max-age=14400). Lighthouse flags it
# as "use efficient cache lifetimes". Static folders below are now immutable/1y.
#
# ⚠️ MAINTENANCE (immutable = 1 year in caches):
#   * CSS change  -> re-hash:  H=$(sha256sum css/style.css | cut -c1-8)
#                   then set  css/style.css?v=$H  in index.html.
#                   A content-hash token can never go stale the way a date can:
#                   the earlier ?v=20260917 was already cached for a year when the
#                   CSS changed again the same day, which would have served a
#                   stylesheet with no @font-face to those visitors.
#   * Image swap  -> use a NEW filename (e.g. katerina-tsiga-2.webp) instead of
#                    overwriting the existing file, or bump ?v= on the reference.
#   * Fonts       -> /fonts/*.woff2 are referenced from style.css, so they are
#                    busted together with the CSS token above.
#   * HTML is deliberately NOT covered here (Pages serves it max-age=0, which is
#     correct: content updates must propagate immediately).
#
# /vendor/* — third-party files we serve ourselves (currently Font Awesome 6.5.1).
# Safe to cache immutably because the VERSION is in the path: a future update
# lands on a new directory (vendor/font-awesome/6.6.0/...), never over these.

# Security headers (18/9/2026) — invisible; added after the weekly check flagged them missing.
#   HSTS: the site is already HTTPS-only (http -> 301); includeSubDomains is safe (only www, which
#   redirects here). Without it the very first plaintext hop is interceptable.
#   X-Frame-Options: nothing embeds this site, so framing it is never legitimate (clickjacking).
#   Permissions-Policy: the page uses none of these browser APIs.
#   CSP (19/10/2026): the old note here said "not added on purpose — the Google Ads tag could break".
#   That was true only because it had never been tested. It now has: the policy below was applied on
#   staging and the page was loaded in a real Chrome with the console watched for CSP violations —
#   zero. The Ads side is covered explicitly (googletagmanager for gtag.js, plus the doubleclick /
#   googleadservices / google hosts that receive the conversion beacon on paid clicks), which is
#   exactly the part a guessed policy would have broken silently.
#   'unsafe-inline' stays for scripts: the page has 18 inline handlers and 30 KB of inline JS, and
#   hashes would break on every copy edit. It does NOT weaken remote-script blocking — the point of
#   the policy is that an injected <script src="evil"> or a hijacked third-party domain is refused.
#   frame-ancestors duplicates X-Frame-Options for browsers that prefer the CSP version.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://www.googletagmanager.com https://www.googleadservices.com https://googleads.g.doubleclick.net https://www.google.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https://www.googletagmanager.com https://www.google-analytics.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://googleads.g.doubleclick.net https://www.google.com https://www.google.gr https://www.facebook.com; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://www.googletagmanager.com https://www.google-analytics.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://googleads.g.doubleclick.net https://stats.g.doubleclick.net https://www.google.com https://www.google.gr; frame-src https://www.googletagmanager.com https://td.doubleclick.net https://www.google.com https://maps.google.com https://www.google.gr; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), magnetometer=()

/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/images/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/vendor/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
